This patch contains some diffs extracted from the Fedora kernel patches, aiming
to improve UEFI secure boot support by more closely replicating the behavior of
of most other modern GNU/Linux distributions which support secure boot.

This includes supporting auto-enabling of lockdown=integrity depending upon
whether or not the system is booted with UEFI secure boot enabled, as well as
supporting module verification for modules which are signed by keys trusted by
the platform (e.g., certificates in UEFI db or MokList), instead of being
solely reliant upon only the kernel's internal trust database.

The original patch source, from which this patch was extracted/isolated from,
can be found at the following URL:

<https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/kernel/blob/f42/f/patch-6.15-redhat.patch>

diff '--color=auto' -apruN a/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c b/arch/x86/kernel/setup.c
